From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:48:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Fix what the world thread review found

audit/2026-11-05/world-threads-review, each with a test (AthenaWorldThreadsReviewTest):
- The JVM's shutdown hook no longer dies before anything is saved: it asks the server thread to stop, and stops the server itself only if that thread is stuck or gone.
- A potion with no effects no longer puts null in the effect cache's ConcurrentHashMap.
- The online player list is read from one snapshot everywhere, not by size and get while other threads shrink it.
- Stronghold and fortress starts run one at a time: their pieces work in statics and shared weights.
- A task queued for a world goes to the world's thread if the world got one meanwhile, also from a thread's hand-back.
- A world keeps its own clock, whichever thread ticks it; furnaces and brewing stands start from it.
- The fireworks recipe's result and the craft view are per thread.

